# FR-250: runs emitrust-bx's pytest suite inside the fast lit tier. It pins
# the bijection laws as PROPERTIES (>= 500 generated Kernel functions, law 1
# and law 2 on the Rust side in pure python and on the C++ side through real
# clang), plus per-module unit tests. Bytecode/cache writes are disabled so a
# test run never dirties the source tree. `-n auto` (pytest-xdist): run
# serially the suite outgrew lit's 600s per-test timeout on CI.
# RUN: env PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 %python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n auto %bx_src/tests
